  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "9eXWGZSkUsIquYDE9C+w9NV+Qkw=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T18:11:49.000Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "Intended outcome (BIM briefing): demonstrate to dtbau that Powerhouse can on-board users and give each an information view **tailored to their role and identity**, aggregating three sources from the existing backup solution:\n\n- **Source 1 \u2014 IFC object hierarchy**, extracted per IFC file, exposed to LLMs as a conceptual snapshot (\"this file has one building with one floor and two rooms with IDs \u2026\")\n- **Source 2 \u2014 BCF comments** carrying IFC object references, joined to Source 1 objects (by GlobalId)\n- **Source 3 \u2014 a PM-level document model** that references and depends on Sources 1 and 2; inspiration: Plannerly's document types (EIR, BEP)\n\nDemo scenario (WIP): a dtbau admin invites the MEPF-responsible manager; on accepting, the manager sees **only** the BCF comments on relevant IFC classes (ducts, pipes, cables) plus related IFC files. User types get their own drive scoped to the documents they should access (PFN\u00dcR project structure).\n\nCross-silo AI work to illustrate: flagging MEPF IFC files with mismatching objects; auto-tagging non-BCF comments related to MEPF work; progress auto-updating in the MEPF section of the PM document.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-14T18:11:49.710774+00:00"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T18:11:49.000Z"
    }
  },
